# Project Conventions

- Keep code clean, readable, and maintainable.
- Prefer simple solutions over unnecessary complexity.
- Preserve existing functionality when modifying code.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Explain important changes briefly after completing a task.
- Test changes when practical.
- Keep documentation updated when project behavior changes.

- Follow Conventional Commits for Git commit messages.